 <h4 class="u_1804382304 dmNewParagraph" data-element-type="paragraph" id="1804382304" style="transition: opacity 1s ease-in-out;"><div style="text-align: center;"><font color="#ffffff"><span style="font-size: 24px; font-weight: 300;"><i>Guest Fellow, Jun - Sep 2022</i></span></font></div></h4> <div class="dmRespRow u_1657779370" id="1657779370"> <div class="dmRespColsWrapper" id="1110127783"> <div class="dmRespCol small-12 medium-12 large-12 u_1713000024" id="1713000024"> <div class="u_1737386924 dmNewParagraph" id="1737386924"><div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">Pengshan Pan's research focuses on international development and political economy, especially in Central and South Asia. In particular, he explores the interlinkages between foreign direct investment, the environment and conflict. At TRANSECT, he is working on the project of China's agricultural production and technology  investments in Pakistan and Kazakhstan.</span></div><div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><br/></span></div><div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><a href="mailto:pep27@pitt.edu" runtime_url="mailto:pep27@pitt.edu">pep27@pitt.edu</a></span></div></div></div> 
